       “ssttaatt oovveerrrriiddeess” are a way to tell ddppkkgg(1) to use a different owner or
       mode for a path when a package is installed (this applies to any
       filesystem object that ddppkkgg handles, including directories, devices,
       etc.). This can be used to force programs that are normally setuid to
       be install without a setuid flag, or only executable by a certain
       group.

       ddppkkgg--ssttaattoovveerrrriiddee is a utility to manage the list of stat overrides. It
       has three basic functions: adding, removing and listing overrides.

